diff --git a/ios/README.md b/ios/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a91c97c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ios/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,78 @@
+# OpenUG2 on iOS
+
+An iOS front end for [OpenUG2](../README.md): SDL2 + OpenGL ES 2.0, on-screen touch controls, game data
+from the app's Documents folder. **You supply your own copy of NFSU2** (OpenUG2 ships no EA assets).
+
+> Status: untested on a device when this was written. It was syntax-checked against the iOS defines only.
+> Expect to fix a few build errors on the first compile; the engine itself is an early prototype
+> (driving, traffic and some races work; there is no full career).
+
+## What you need
+- A Mac (a Hackintosh is fine) with Xcode and its command line tools
+- `brew install cmake xcodegen`
+- An iPhone/iPad with iOS 13 or newer
+- The NFSU2 files from your own DVD/install: the folders OpenUG2 reads (`TRACKS/`, `CARS/`, and the rest of
+  the data directory the desktop build is pointed at)
+
+## 1. Build the libraries (once)
+```sh
+cd ios
+./build_deps.sh                         # device (arm64): SDL2 + libpng -> deps/out/iphoneos
+SDK=iphonesimulator ./build_deps.sh     # optional, Apple-silicon simulator
+```
+SHA-256 comes from Apple's CommonCrypto (`compat/openssl/sha.h`), so there is no OpenSSL to build.
+
+## 2. Generate the Xcode project and build
+```sh
+xcodegen generate
+open OpenUG2.xcodeproj
+```
+In Xcode: select the **OpenUG2** target, **Signing & Capabilities**, choose your Team and change the bundle
+identifier to something unique (a free Apple ID works). Pick your device and Run. The scheme builds
+**Release** on purpose: the engine is far too slow unoptimised.
+
+## 3. Put the game data on the device
+The app's **Documents** folder is the data directory and the working directory (settings and key bindings
+are written there too).
+- Finder (macOS): select the iPhone, **Files** tab, drag your NFSU2 folders onto **OpenUG2**
+- or the **Files** app: *On My iPhone > OpenUG2*
+
+The default car and track are the engine's defaults (`CARS/HUMMER`, `TRACKS/STREAML4RA`), so those must be
+present. The start menu offers **Free Roam** and **Race Select**.
+
+## Controls
+| Where | What |
+|---|---|
+| Left strip | Steering: slide your finger left/right of the strip's centre (analog) |
+| Bottom right | **GAS** (big, corner), **BRK**, **NOS**, **HB** (handbrake) |
+| Top row | **PAUSE**, **CAM**, **RESET**, **LOOK** (look back) |
+| Menus (start + pause) | D-pad on the left, **OK** and **BACK** on the right |
+
+The buttons send whatever keys the Controls screen has bound, so rebinding there still works. A Bluetooth
+controller works too (SDL game controller support is on).
+
+## Installing without Xcode on every refresh
+A free Apple ID signs apps for **7 days** and allows 3 active sideloaded apps; that is an Apple rule, not
+something this project can change. Options:
+
+1. **Unsigned IPA + a sideloading tool.** `./make_ipa.sh` writes `build/OpenUG2-unsigned.ipa`. Install it
+   with SideStore, AltStore or Sideloadly, which re-sign it with your own Apple ID.
+   - SideStore refreshes in the background on the device itself after a one-time computer-assisted setup
+     (it needs the LocalDevVPN app). Free accounts: 3 active apps (SideStore counts as one), 10 App IDs
+     per week. See <https://docs.sidestore.io/docs/faq>.
+   - AltStore Classic also works with a free Apple ID (3 active apps): <https://faq.altstore.io/altstore-classic/activating-apps>.
+2. **Paid Apple Developer account ($99/year):** apps last 365 days and the 3-app limit goes away.
+3. Plain Xcode with a free account: works, but you must re-run it every 7 days.
+
+## Settings worth knowing
+- `OPENUG2_IOS_HIGHDPI=1` (in `project.yml`): render at native Retina pixels. Default is points, because
+  the world draws ~930 m of view and fill rate is the first limit on a phone.
+- GL ES 2.0 is deprecated by Apple but still works (`GLES_SILENCE_DEPRECATION` is set). If a future iOS
+  drops it, the fallback is ANGLE (GLES2 on top of Metal).
+- Textures are CPU-decoded to RGBA: iOS GPUs have no S3TC, and the engine already has this fallback.
+  Expect higher memory use than desktop.
+
+## What changed in the engine
+Everything is behind `#ifdef OPENUG2_IOS` / `OPENUG2_TOUCH`, so desktop builds are unchanged:
+`src/main.c` (hooks), `src/controls_sdl.c` (two queries ask the touch layer), plus the new
+`src/touch_ios.[ch]`, `ios/ios_platform.[hm]` and `ios/compat/`.
diff --git a/ios/build_deps.sh b/ios/build_deps.sh
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..9b5e8cd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ios/build_deps.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+#!/bin/bash
+# Builds the two libraries OpenUG2 needs, as static iOS libraries, into ios/deps/out/<sdk>/:
+#   SDL2    (windowing, GLES context, touch, audio, game controllers) -- SDL's own "Static Library-iOS" target
+#   libpng  (UI glyph/button images) -- CMake; zlib comes from the iOS SDK
+# SHA-256 (the only OpenSSL use) is served by CommonCrypto through ios/compat, so there is no libcrypto.
+#
+# Usage:  ./build_deps.sh                       device (arm64)
+#         SDK=iphonesimulator ./build_deps.sh   Apple-silicon simulator
+# Needs:  Xcode command line tools, cmake, git (brew install cmake)
+set -euo pipefail
+cd "$(dirname "$0")"
+
+SDK=${SDK:-iphoneos}
+DEPLOY=${DEPLOY:-13.0}
+SDL_TAG=${SDL_TAG:-release-2.30.12}
+PNG_TAG=${PNG_TAG:-v1.6.43}
+
+case "$SDK" in iphoneos|iphonesimulator) ;; *) echo "SDK must be iphoneos or iphonesimulator" >&2; exit 1;; esac
+command -v cmake >/dev/null || { echo "cmake not found: brew install cmake" >&2; exit 1; }
+
+ROOT=$PWD
+SRC=$ROOT/deps/src
+BUILD=$ROOT/deps/build
+OUT=$ROOT/deps/out/$SDK
+SDKPATH=$(xcrun --sdk "$SDK" --show-sdk-path)
+mkdir -p "$SRC" "$BUILD" "$OUT/lib" "$OUT/include"
+
+fetch() {   # name url tag
+    [ -d "$SRC/$1/.git" ] || git clone --depth 1 --branch "$3" "$2" "$SRC/$1"
+}
+
+echo "== SDL2 ($SDL_TAG) for $SDK"
+fetch SDL https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL.git "$SDL_TAG"
+xcodebuild -project "$SRC/SDL/Xcode/SDL/SDL.xcodeproj" -target "Static Library-iOS" \
+    -configuration Release -sdk "$SDK" ARCHS=arm64 ONLY_ACTIVE_ARCH=NO \
+    IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET="$DEPLOY" BUILD_DIR="$BUILD/sdl-$SDK" \
+    CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO build | tail -n 5
+LIBSDL=$(find "$BUILD/sdl-$SDK" -name libSDL2.a | head -n 1)
+[ -n "$LIBSDL" ] || { echo "libSDL2.a was not produced" >&2; exit 1; }
+cp "$LIBSDL" "$OUT/lib/libSDL2.a"
+
+echo "== libpng ($PNG_TAG) for $SDK"
+fetch libpng https://github.com/pnggroup/libpng.git "$PNG_TAG"
+cmake -S "$SRC/libpng" -B "$BUILD/png-$SDK" \
+    -DCMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME=iOS -DCMAKE_OSX_SYSROOT="$SDK" -DCMAKE_OSX_ARCHITECTURES=arm64 \
+    -DCMAKE_OSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET="$DEPLOY" -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
+    -DCMAKE_TRY_COMPILE_TARGET_TYPE=STATIC_LIBRARY \
+    -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX="$OUT" \
+    -DZLIB_LIBRARY="$SDKPATH/usr/lib/libz.tbd" -DZLIB_INCLUDE_DIR="$SDKPATH/usr/include" \
+    -DPNG_SHARED=OFF -DPNG_STATIC=ON -DPNG_TESTS=OFF -DPNG_TOOLS=OFF -DPNG_EXECUTABLES=OFF -DPNG_FRAMEWORK=OFF
+cmake --build "$BUILD/png-$SDK" --config Release --target install -j 4
+# the static library is installed as libpng16.a with a libpng.a alias; make sure the name we link exists
+[ -f "$OUT/lib/libpng16.a" ] || cp "$(find "$OUT/lib" -name 'libpng*.a' | head -n 1)" "$OUT/lib/libpng16.a"
+
+echo "== done: $OUT"
+ls -la "$OUT/lib"
diff --git a/ios/compat/openssl/sha.h b/ios/compat/openssl/sha.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8d370dd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ios/compat/openssl/sha.h
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+/* compat/openssl/sha.h -- iOS shim: the only OpenSSL call OpenUG2 makes is SHA256()
+ * (src/ugui/ugui_glyph_folder.c), so on iOS it is served by Apple's CommonCrypto
+ * instead of building and linking libcrypto. Put ios/compat on the header search
+ * path BEFORE any system include path. */
+#ifndef OPENUG2_IOS_COMPAT_OPENSSL_SHA_H
+#define OPENUG2_IOS_COMPAT_OPENSSL_SHA_H
+
+#include <CommonCrypto/CommonDigest.h>
+#include <stddef.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
+
+#define SHA256_DIGEST_LENGTH CC_SHA256_DIGEST_LENGTH
+
+/* Same contract as OpenSSL's: writes 32 bytes to md and returns md, or NULL on failure. */
+static inline unsigned char *SHA256(const unsigned char *d, size_t n, unsigned char *md) {
+    if (!md || (!d && n) || n > (size_t)UINT32_MAX) return NULL;   /* CC_LONG is 32 bit */
+    CC_SHA256(d, (CC_LONG)n, md);
+    return md;
+}
+
+#endif
diff --git a/ios/gen_headers.sh b/ios/gen_headers.sh
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..df70cfb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ios/gen_headers.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# Regenerates src/generated_shaders.h and src/generated_world_debug_shaders.h: the same output as the
+# Makefile rules of those names (the desktop build makes them with xxd; macOS ships xxd too).
+# Skips the work when both headers are newer than every shader, so incremental Xcode builds stay fast.
+set -eu
+cd "$(dirname "$0")/.."
+command -v xxd >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo "gen_headers: xxd not found" >&2; exit 1; }
+
+up_to_date() {   # $1 = header, rest = inputs
+    out=$1; shift
+    [ -f "$out" ] || return 1
+    for f in "$@"; do [ "$f" -nt "$out" ] && return 1; done
+    return 0
+}
+
+SHADERS=$(ls src/shaders/*.vert src/shaders/*.frag | sort)
+
+if ! up_to_date src/generated_world_debug_shaders.h src/world_debug_120.vert src/world_debug_120.frag; then
+    {
+        echo "/* AUTO-GENERATED from world_debug_120.vert/.frag by make -- do not edit */"
+        xxd -i src/world_debug_120.vert
+        xxd -i src/world_debug_120.frag
+    } > src/generated_world_debug_shaders.h
+fi
+
+# shellcheck disable=SC2086
+if ! up_to_date src/generated_shaders.h $SHADERS; then
+    {
+        echo "/* AUTO-GENERATED from src/shaders/ by make -- do not edit */"
+        for f in $SHADERS; do xxd -i "$f" | sed 's/^unsigned/static const unsigned/'; done
+    } > src/generated_shaders.h
+fi
diff --git a/ios/ios_platform.h b/ios/ios_platform.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e749874
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ios/ios_platform.h
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+/* ios_platform.h -- the small iOS layer around the engine (compiled only for iOS, -DOPENUG2_IOS).
+ *
+ * The engine is a command-line program: it takes the NFSU2 data directory as an argument and keeps its
+ * settings and output files in the working directory. An iOS app has neither, so this layer
+ *   - points the data directory and the working directory at the app's Documents folder (visible in the
+ *     Files app because the Info.plist enables file sharing -- copy the game's TRACKS/, CARS/, ... there);
+ *   - sets the SDL hints that have to be set before SDL_Init (landscape only, hidden home indicator);
+ *   - stops all GL work while the app is in the background (iOS terminates apps that draw there). */
+#ifndef OPENUG2_IOS_PLATFORM_H
+#define OPENUG2_IOS_PLATFORM_H
+
+#include <SDL.h>
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+extern "C" {
+#endif
+
+/* Call first thing in main(), before SDL_Init. Sets the SDL hints, chdir()s into Documents and returns that
+ * directory (valid for the life of the process; never NULL -- "." if the lookup failed). */
+const char *ios_platform_init(void);
+
+/* Feed every SDL event through this. On SDL_APP_WILLENTERBACKGROUND it blocks until the app is foreground
+ * again (or quits), so the render loop makes no GL call while backgrounded. Returns 1 if it blocked. */
+int ios_platform_event(const SDL_Event *e);
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+}
+#endif
+
+/* Extra SDL_CreateWindow flags for iOS: full screen. Retina rendering is opt-in because the world draws
+ * ~930 m of view and fill rate is the first thing a phone runs out of: build with
+ * OPENUG2_IOS_HIGHDPI=1 to render at native pixels instead of points. */
+#ifdef OPENUG2_IOS_HIGHDPI
+#  define OPENUG2_EXTRA_WINDOW_FLAGS (SDL_WINDOW_FULLSCREEN | SDL_WINDOW_BORDERLESS | SDL_WINDOW_ALLOW_HIGHDPI)
+#else
+#  define OPENUG2_EXTRA_WINDOW_FLAGS (SDL_WINDOW_FULLSCREEN | SDL_WINDOW_BORDERLESS)
+#endif
+
+#endif
diff --git a/ios/ios_platform.m b/ios/ios_platform.m
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..bdbbef5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ios/ios_platform.m
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+/* ios_platform.m -- see ios_platform.h */
+#import <Foundation/Foundation.h>
+#include <string.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
+
+#include "ios_platform.h"
+
+static char g_docs[1024];
+
+const char *ios_platform_init(void) {
+    /* Hints are read when the video subsystem starts, so they go in before SDL_Init. */
+    SDL_SetHint(SDL_HINT_ORIENTATIONS, "LandscapeLeft LandscapeRight");
+    SDL_SetHint(SDL_HINT_IOS_HIDE_HOME_INDICATOR, "2");        /* hidden, swipe once to reveal */
+    SDL_SetHint(SDL_HINT_TOUCH_MOUSE_EVENTS, "0");             /* touches drive the on-screen controls only, not the mouse path */
+    SDL_SetHint(SDL_HINT_ACCELEROMETER_AS_JOYSTICK, "0");      /* else SDL lists the accelerometer as a pad */
+
+    @autoreleasepool {
+        NSArray<NSString *> *dirs = NSSearchPathForDirectoriesInDomains(NSDocumentDirectory, NSUserDomainMask, YES);
+        const char *p = dirs.count ? dirs[0].fileSystemRepresentation : NULL;
+        if (p && strlen(p) < sizeof g_docs) strcpy(g_docs, p);
+    }
+    if (!g_docs[0]) { strcpy(g_docs, "."); return g_docs; }
+
+    /* Settings, controls and any file the engine writes with a relative path land in Documents too. */
+    if (chdir(g_docs) != 0) perror("openug2: chdir(Documents)");
+    return g_docs;
+}
+
+int ios_platform_event(const SDL_Event *e) {
+    if (e->type != SDL_APP_WILLENTERBACKGROUND) return 0;
+    /* SDL delivers this on the UI thread right before iOS suspends us. Any GL call after it kills the app,
+       so wait here -- inside the event handler, before the frame loop gets to draw again. */
+    SDL_Event ev;
+    while (SDL_WaitEvent(&ev)) {
+        if (ev.type == SDL_APP_DIDENTERFOREGROUND || ev.type == SDL_QUIT || ev.type == SDL_APP_TERMINATING) {
+            if (ev.type != SDL_APP_DIDENTERFOREGROUND) SDL_PushEvent(&ev);   /* let the loop see the quit */
+            break;
+        }
+    }
+    return 1;
+}
diff --git a/ios/make_ipa.sh b/ios/make_ipa.sh
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..9de9d9c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ios/make_ipa.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# Builds an UNSIGNED .ipa (ios/build/OpenUG2-unsigned.ipa) for sideloading tools -- AltStore, SideStore,
+# Sideloadly -- which sign it with your own Apple ID, so no Xcode run is needed on each refresh.
+# Run ./build_deps.sh first (device libraries), and `xcodegen generate` once.
+set -eu
+cd "$(dirname "$0")"
+[ -d OpenUG2.xcodeproj ] || xcodegen generate
+xcodebuild -project OpenUG2.xcodeproj -scheme OpenUG2 -configuration Release \
+    -sdk iphoneos -destination 'generic/platform=iOS' -derivedDataPath build \
+    CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO CODE_SIGNING_REQUIRED=NO CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY="" build
+APP=build/Build/Products/Release-iphoneos/OpenUG2.app
+[ -d "$APP" ] || { echo "build did not produce $APP" >&2; exit 1; }
+rm -rf build/ipa build/OpenUG2-unsigned.ipa
+mkdir -p build/ipa/Payload
+cp -R "$APP" build/ipa/Payload/
+( cd build/ipa && zip -qry ../OpenUG2-unsigned.ipa Payload )
+echo "wrote $(pwd)/build/OpenUG2-unsigned.ipa"
diff --git a/ios/project.yml b/ios/project.yml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6603963
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ios/project.yml
@@ -0,0 +1,95 @@
+# XcodeGen spec -- `brew install xcodegen && xcodegen generate` (in this folder) writes OpenUG2.xcodeproj.
+name: OpenUG2
+options:
+  bundleIdPrefix: com.example          # change me, or set the bundle id in Signing & Capabilities
+  deploymentTarget:
+    iOS: "13.0"
+  createIntermediateGroups: true
+  generateEmptyDirectories: false
+
+targets:
+  OpenUG2:
+    type: application
+    platform: iOS
+    sources:
+      - path: ../src                   # the engine: C99, no changes needed beyond the OPENUG2_* hooks
+        includes: ["**/*.c", "**/*.h"]
+        excludes:
+          - "rhi_vk.c"                 # Vulkan backend: offscreen-only for now
+          - "vk_offscreen_window_shim.c"
+          - "vk_ui_stubs.c"
+      - path: ios_platform.m
+      - path: ios_platform.h
+    preBuildScripts:
+      - name: Generate embedded shader headers
+        script: '"${SRCROOT}/gen_headers.sh"'
+        basedOnDependencyAnalysis: false
+    info:
+      path: Info.plist
+      properties:
+        CFBundleDisplayName: OpenUG2
+        CFBundleShortVersionString: "0.1"
+        CFBundleVersion: "1"
+        UIFileSharingEnabled: true               # Documents shows up in Finder / Files: copy the game data there
+        LSSupportsOpeningDocumentsInPlace: true
+        UIRequiresFullScreen: true
+        UIStatusBarHidden: true
+        UIViewControllerBasedStatusBarAppearance: false
+        UILaunchScreen: {}
+        UISupportedInterfaceOrientations:
+          - UIInterfaceOrientationLandscapeLeft
+          - UIInterfaceOrientationLandscapeRight
+        UIApplicationSupportsIndirectInputEvents: true
+        ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption: false
+    settings:
+      base:
+        PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER: com.example.openug2
+        TARGETED_DEVICE_FAMILY: "1,2"
+        GCC_C_LANGUAGE_STANDARD: gnu99            # the Makefile's -std=c99 plus _DEFAULT_SOURCE
+        CLANG_ENABLE_OBJC_ARC: YES
+        ENABLE_USER_SCRIPT_SANDBOXING: NO         # gen_headers.sh writes into ../src
+        GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS:
+          - N2_GLES=1                             # OpenGL ES 2.0 backend (+ GLSL ES shaders)
+          - OPENUG2_IOS=1
+          - OPENUG2_TOUCH=1
+          - OPENUG2_MENU=1                        # start menu (free roam / race select): no command line on iOS
+          - GLES_SILENCE_DEPRECATION=1
+          # - OPENUG2_IOS_HIGHDPI=1               # render at native Retina pixels (heavier)
+          - $(inherited)
+        GCC_WARN_INHIBIT_ALL_WARNINGS: NO
+        OTHER_CFLAGS: ["-Wno-unused-function"]
+        HEADER_SEARCH_PATHS:
+          - "$(SRCROOT)/compat"                   # openssl/sha.h -> CommonCrypto, must come first
+          - "$(SRCROOT)"
+          - "$(SRCROOT)/../src"
+          - "$(SRCROOT)/deps/src/SDL/include"
+          - "$(SRCROOT)/deps/out/$(PLATFORM_NAME)/include"
+        LIBRARY_SEARCH_PATHS:
+          - "$(SRCROOT)/deps/out/$(PLATFORM_NAME)/lib"
+        OTHER_LDFLAGS: ["-lSDL2", "-lpng16", "-lz", "-lm", "-ObjC"]
+        ONLY_ACTIVE_ARCH: NO
+    dependencies:
+      - sdk: AudioToolbox.framework
+      - sdk: AVFoundation.framework
+      - sdk: CoreAudio.framework
+      - sdk: CoreBluetooth.framework
+      - sdk: CoreGraphics.framework
+      - sdk: CoreHaptics.framework
+      - sdk: CoreMotion.framework
+      - sdk: CoreVideo.framework
+      - sdk: Foundation.framework
+      - sdk: GameController.framework
+      - sdk: Metal.framework
+      - sdk: OpenGLES.framework
+      - sdk: QuartzCore.framework
+      - sdk: UIKit.framework
+
+schemes:
+  OpenUG2:
+    build:
+      targets:
+        OpenUG2: all
+    run:
+      config: Release          # the engine is far too slow in an unoptimised Debug build
+    archive:
+      config: Release
